  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 7% permanent limit (above the 5% answer-key ceiling) with no sales stop, no transition cap, and no exemption, while keeping per-model results regulator-confidential and provided to purchasers. S3 drops any retrofit obligation for installed units (only disclosure and isolation instructions), which benefits Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage, and sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months. S5 makes recall mandatory at 8 per 100,000 with no transition window and relies on regulator confirmation, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) to an immediate trigger; S4 at 36 months and S1 reporting timelines fall within the acceptable range."
 },
